>pet/bag: The Luggage ! It is based on Terry Pratchett's Discworld
>novels. In the series there is a tourist named Twoflower who has
>this magical trunk with him. The Luggage follows him with his
>hundreds of little legs, and can even attack monsters.
>The Luggage seems to be able to carry a large number of
>things (bag of carrying), but unfortunately it can't be
>opened if it doesn't want to open.
>When killed, it could polymorph into an ordinary suitcase/bag/bag of carrying
>or even be destroyed...
>
>Well, what do you think ?

Not a bad idea!  Better yet, it brings to mind another one.

Twoflower, on the cover of one of the Discworld paperbacks,
is _riding_ The Luggage through the air.  For those times
when the xans have got your gams, being able to _ride_ a
sufficiently large pet would sure be handy.  If one also had
found a bridle, it might be possible to control where ones
pet was going, rather than the default "whither thou goest"
mode of riding.

Riding a pet xorn could have some really interesting
consequences, as with several other pets.  Riding a tame
trapper that had just become hungry and untame would have
the "lady riding the tiger" results, you'd end up inside!

This provides a possible whole new dimension for nethack
3.1, with lots of code needed to make it work.

Comments? 

